1 NOTE Compiled from Dutch civil registry (BHIC), FamilySearch, and family documents. Seven generations traced from Petrus van Duijnhoven (b.1799 Uden) through modern descendants in USA and Netherlands. WISCONSIN VAN DYN HOVEN BRANCH NOTE: A separate branch of Van Dyn Hoven families flourishes in the Fox Valley of Wisconsin (Little Chute, Kaukauna, Appleton, Combined Locks) using the spelling "Van Dyn Hoven" (three words). Little Chute was settled in 1848 by Dutch Catholics from Noord-Brabant led by Dominican missionary Father Theodore J. van den Broek — who came from Uden, the same town as Arthur's paternal ancestors. The connection between the Wisconsin Van Dyn Hoven families and Arthur's Uden/Boekel line has NOT yet been genealogically confirmed, but both share the same Noord-Brabant Catholic origins. The Wisconsin branch is documented separately in WISCONSIN_VAN_DYN_HOVEN_BRANCH.md.
