1 RELI Roman Catholic
1 NOTE Generation 3 patriarch. Son of Martinus and Geertruda Verwegen. Birth akte: BHIC Uden no.44, 24 Apr 1872 (bhi:1230f2d0-e317-ad17-e4b4-dbeff02a38c6). Marriage akte: BHIC Boekel no.9, 18 May 1906 (bhi:92ef5014-4911-89fe-9f0a-d2713aecdd63). Death akte: BHIC Uden no.86, 20 May 1949. Married Anna Maria van den Elzen 18 May 1906 in Boekel, the bride's hometown - a traditional practice in Catholic Brabant where weddings were held in the bride's parish church. Father of 12 children (1907-1923), exemplifying the large Catholic families typical of the "Rijke Roomse Leven" (Rich Roman Life) era in Brabant when families of 10-15 children were common among devout Catholics. Marianus lived his entire 77 years in the deeply Catholic farming community of eastern Brabant. Uden was an agricultural market town where sandy heathlands were being transformed into productive farmland through cooperative effort. The family likely attended the Sint-Petrus church, the heart of Catholic life in Uden. In 1848, Dominican Father Theodore van den Broek had led Dutch Catholics from Uden to Wisconsin, beginning a pattern of emigration that Marianus's own son Johan would follow a century later. Marianus witnessed the German occupation (May 1940 - September 1944) and lived through Uden's liberation on 17 September 1944 during Operation Market Garden, the massive Allied airborne operation. He died 20 May 1949, just four and a half years after liberation, having seen his homeland freed at age 77.
