1 NOTE Tenth child, fourth daughter. Born September 1919, just months after WWI ended - while the Netherlands remained neutral, the war years (1914-1918) brought food shortages and economic hardship even to non-combatant nations. The family survived WWI intact: father Marianus was 42-46 during the war (too old for service even if the Netherlands had mobilized), and the older sons were still children. Gerarda Maria's name combines the popular Brabant name 'Gerarda' with 'Maria' honoring the Virgin Mary - a common Catholic compound name structure.
