1 NOTE Eleventh child, seventh son. Name variant of father's name Marianus - following the Dutch Catholic tradition of naming a later son after the father (earlier sons honored grandfathers). Marinus was born November 1920, making him 20 years old when the Germans invaded in May 1940 and 24 at liberation in September 1944. As a young man during the occupation, he would have been at risk for the 'Arbeitseinsatz' (forced labor in German factories) that affected many Dutch men his age. The Uden area was liberated by Allied forces during Operation Market Garden in September 1944.
