1 NOTE Generation 6. Second child of Peter John and Mary Campbell. US+Dutch dual citizen. Lives in Haarlem, Noord-Holland, Netherlands — a city of 165,000 people just 20 km west of Amsterdam, known as "the gateway to the bulb fields" (de poort naar de bollenstreek). Haarlem's Grote Markt, dominated by the 15th-century Sint-Bavokerk where Mozart played the organ, is one of the most beautiful market squares in the Netherlands. The city boasts the Frans Hals Museum (named for the Golden Age portrait painter who lived there) and is surrounded by the Bollenstreek tulip region that draws millions of visitors each spring. Arthur's move to Haarlem in the 2010s represents a remarkable return migration — his great-grandfather Johan left Noord-Brabant in 1950, and now the 6th generation has returned to Dutch soil. Previously married to Merel (divorced). Father of Raven and Starling (Generation 7), both US+Dutch dual citizens growing up bilingual in Dutch and English. Compiler of this family tree.
