1 NOTE Generation 3. Son of Martinus van Duijnhoven (Gen 2) and Geertruda Verwegen, born 16 Dec 1865 in Uden. Elder brother of Marianus (1872, direct ancestor). Antonius led a remarkable life spanning both World Wars and two marriages. FIRST MARRIAGE (~1895): Lamberdina van Dijk, who died circa 1901. From this marriage: Josephus Antonius (1905), Joannes Petrus Paulus (1906 - unusually born in Helmond), Gerardus Petrus (1908), Adrianus Antonius (1909-1972). SECOND MARRIAGE (Feb 1903): Antonia Vermulst, married in Uden about 18 months after first wife's death. From this marriage: Josina Maria (1910), Johanna Maria (1912), Theodora Josephina (1915), Petrus Hubertus (1917 - died young 22 Jul 1931 age 14), Maria (1920), Louisa Antonia (1923). At least 13 confirmed children total (10 confirmed, possibly 3 more). This large family exemplifies the "kinderrijk gezin" (child-rich family) ideal promoted by the Catholic Church in Brabant during the "Rijke Roomse Leven" era. Antonius's children born 1905-1923 lived through WWI (though Netherlands was neutral), the interwar Depression, and WWII German occupation. This Dutch branch represents second cousins of Johan/John van Duijnhoven (Gen 4, Arthur's grandfather).
1 FAMC @F002@
