1 RELI Roman Catholic
1 NOTE Generation -1. Father of Petrus van Duijnhoven (1799, Gen1 @I001@). Married Elisabeth Henricus van Boxtel on 30 Nov 1796. HISTORICAL CONTEXT: Petrus Johannes lived through one of the most turbulent periods in Dutch history. Born in 1748 during the declining years of the Dutch Golden Age, he witnessed the French Revolution's shockwaves reach the Netherlands. He died on 26 July 1799 - just four years after French troops invaded Brabant (January 1795) and established the Batavian Republic, ending 147 years of Catholic oppression in the Generality Lands. His son Petrus was born posthumously (27 August 1799, exactly one month after his death) - a poignant detail: the father who lived his entire life as a second-class citizen in his own homeland never saw his son grow up in the new republic that finally granted Catholics equal rights. His father Joannes Peter had died just 4 years earlier (1795), meaning the family lost two patriarchs in rapid succession during this revolutionary era. Source: Van Elk genealogy tree (genealogieonline.nl/genealogie-van-elk), ref I6927.php.
1 FAMC @F018@
1 FAMS @F017@

