1 NOTE Generation -2. Father of Petrus Johannes (1748, Gen -1). Married Allegondis Janssen van den Bout (van Haandel). Had siblings: Johannes (1720-1792), Jacobus (~1722, possible twin, died age 25), Antonius (1727-1754). Father was Petrus Jansen van Duijnhoven (1679). HISTORICAL CONTEXT: Born around 1722, Joannes Peter lived his entire 73 years under the oppressive Generality Lands regime. Since the Peace of Westphalia (1648), Catholic Brabant had been ruled as a conquered territory by the Protestant Dutch Republic - Catholics could not hold public office, practice their faith openly, or send children to Catholic schools. Churches were confiscated; worship happened in hidden 'schuurkerken' (barn churches). He died in May 1795, just months after French Revolutionary troops liberated Brabant (January 1795) and ended this 147-year humiliation. Tragically, he likely did not live to see the full emancipation that followed. His 5 children including son Petrus Johannes (1748) and 'Jean' (1757, who had 8 children) carried the family through this pivotal transition. Source: Van Elk genealogy tree, Bernards tree.
1 FAMC @F020@
1 FAMS @F018@

