1 NOTE Joseph Ortscheid x Teresa McDonald — parents of Mary Ellen Ortscheid (@I118@), Mary Cecilia Campbell's maternal grandparents. The Ortscheid-McDonald union represents the intermarriage of German-Catholic and Irish-Catholic families in the lead-mining region of southwestern Wisconsin. Cuba City, their home, lies at the heart of the Upper Mississippi Valley Mining District where lead and zinc mining drove the local economy from the 1820s through the mid-20th century. Their daughter Mary Ellen (b.4 Jul 1919 Cuba City) left this mining-town background to become a teacher and eventually settled in Red Wing, Minnesota, where she married Fairman Campbell and raised 16 children.

