1 NOTE Mother of Wilhelmus Cornelissen (b.7 Dec 1876 Bakel en Milheeze), grandmother of Anna Maria Cornelissen (wife of Johan van Duijnhoven). The Verhoeven surname is common in Noord-Brabant, and Johanna was part of the Catholic farming community in Bakel en Milheeze — a village that lies east of Helmond on the edge of the Peel, an area of former peat bogs that was being transformed into productive farmland during the 19th century. Married Peter Cornelissen. Their grandson Anna Maria Cornelissen (b.1916) would emigrate to Minnesota with her husband Johan van Duijnhoven in 1950. BHIC source: bhi:71f5efca-7a04-d26d-602d-26e3d76c66bf
