2 SOUR https://www.openarchieven.nl/bhi:71f5efca-7a04-d26d-602d-26e3d76c66bf
1 OCCU Farmer/Agricultural worker
1 RELI Roman Catholic
1 NOTE Father of Anna Maria Cornelissen (b.30 Sep 1916, wife of Johan van Duijnhoven, Arthur's grandmother). Born 7 December 1876 in Bakel en Milheeze — a small agricultural village in the eastern part of Noord-Brabant, near Helmond. The village lies on the edge of the Peel, an area of former peat bogs that was being transformed into productive farmland during this era. Bakel became a separate parish in 1677 and remained deeply Catholic throughout the Protestant-dominated Dutch Republic, benefiting from its proximity to the Catholic enclave of Ravenstein. The 16th century St. Willibrordus Church — the oldest in the area — was the center of village religious life. Parents: Peter Cornelissen x Johanna Verhoeven. Wilhelmus married Anna Maria Verbruggen (~1905-1906) and had approximately 10 children between 1906-1922, including Anna Maria Cornelissen (1916) who would emigrate to America with her husband Johan van Duijnhoven in 1950. The Cornelissen and Verbruggen families were part of the tight-knit Catholic farming community of Bakel en Milheeze, where large families were the norm and agriculture — increasingly intensive pig farming — dominated the local economy. BHIC confirmed.
1 FAMC @F036@
1 FAMS @F037@

