1 NOTE Mother of Anna Maria Cornelissen (b.30 Sep 1916, wife of Johan van Duijnhoven, Arthur's grandmother). Born 14 October 1877 in Bakel en Milheeze, a village in the Land van Cuijk region of eastern Noord-Brabant. Parents: Martinus Verbruggen (son of Gerit Verbruggen x Maria Evers) x Petronella van Grootel (daughter of Joannis Wilhelmus van Grootel x Johanna Bukkems). The Verbruggen family were Catholic farming people who worked the sandy soils of the Peel region, which during the late 19th century was undergoing significant transformation as peat bogs were drained and converted to agricultural land. Anna Maria married Wilhelmus Cornelissen circa 1905-1906 and together they raised approximately 10 children in Bakel en Milheeze between 1906-1922 — a family size typical of Catholic farming families in this region, where children provided essential labor for agricultural work and large families were encouraged by the Church. Her brother Gerardus Verbruggen was born 24 December 1872. Her daughter Anna Maria Cornelissen (1916) would become part of the massive Dutch post-war emigration wave, marrying Johan van Duijnhoven and emigrating to Minnesota in 1950. BHIC confirmed.
