1 NOTE Peter Cornelissen x Johanna Verhoeven — parents of Wilhelmus Cornelissen (b.7 Dec 1876), grandparents of Anna Maria Cornelissen (wife of Johan van Duijnhoven), great-grandparents of Arthur van Duynhoven's father Peter John. The Cornelissen and Verhoeven families were part of the Catholic farming community in Bakel en Milheeze, a village in the Land van Cuijk region of eastern Noord-Brabant. This area remained deeply Catholic even during the Protestant-dominated Dutch Republic, and the 16th century St. Willibrordus Church — the oldest in the region — served as the center of village religious and social life. Their son Wilhelmus (b.1876) would marry Anna Maria Verbruggen (b.1877) and have approximately 10 children between 1906-1922. Bakel en Milheeze, Noord-Brabant.

