1 NOTE WISCONSIN VAN DYN HOVEN BRANCH (connection to Arthur's Uden/Boekel line NOT yet genealogically confirmed, but both share Noord-Brabant Catholic origins). Jerry Van Dyn Hoven (1954-2020) owned Van Dyn Hoven Imports auto dealership in Kaukauna WI, sold to Bergstrom Automotive 2009, later developed hotels. Covered in Post-Crescent newspaper business section. Son of Wilbert Van Dyn Hoven. The Wisconsin Van Dyn Hoven families flourish in the Fox Valley (Little Chute, Kaukauna, Appleton, Combined Locks) using the spelling "Van Dyn Hoven" (three words). This area was settled in 1848 by Dutch Catholics from Noord-Brabant led by Dominican missionary Father Theodore J. van den Broek, who came from Uden — the same town as Arthur's paternal ancestors.

